igin_availability_confirmed, but does not change node ready/occupied status. So we need node ready and occupied simultaneously? That seems contradictory because node ready likely means not occupied? But maybe ready means prepared for loading/unloading, and occupied means has cargo? Could be both true? The predicates may not be mutually exclusive. The precondition of lock includes origin_node_ready and not origin_node_occupied. So after lock, node remains ready and not occupied. Then loading payload makes node occupied but maybe still ready? There's no precondition that ready changes. So after loading, node could be both ready and occupied (if ready not unset). There's no action that unset ready. So we can have both ready and occupied after loading. Good.)
