ue, origin_availability_locked true, cargo_available false (since consumed). For unload we need cargo_available? Actually unload precondition does not require cargo_available; it requires origin_payload_linked, origin_node_occupied, not origin_availability_confirmed. It also requires candidate_prepared, candidate_task_profile_linked, origin_availability_node_linked. After load, we have candidate_prepared? Yes origin_availability_alpha is candidate_prepared? Initially not; we need to make it prepared. We'll need to do confirm_candidate_preparedness for origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha. Also need candidate_task_profile_linked for them. So we need to attach route_task_profile to them.)
